missing_customer_input.description:
Grid costs cannot be calculated until these home profile questions are answered in the Smart Home Solutions customer portal:

{questions}

Open the portal, go to Home profile, answer them and save. This integration picks it up within the hour, or immediately if you reload it.

optimisation_configuration.description:
The 15-minute planner is paused because these explicit inputs are missing or invalid:

{inputs}

Open Configure on this integration. Baseline controllers continue to own the devices while planning is unavailable.

device_control_mapping.description:
The website requests control mappings for these devices:

{devices}

Open Configure on this integration. It fetches the latest website selections immediately; no Home Assistant restart is required. Until each matching mapping is complete, that device remains in empirical base load and existing controllers remain unchanged.

unplanned_service.description:
The equipment below is set up in Home Assistant, but no meter on the Smart Home Solutions website is set to control it, so the planner never sees it:

{services}

Nothing is broken and the rest of the plan is unaffected, but the service contributes nothing: it wins no energy and appears in no schedule. The SHS Energy configuration panel shows this at the top of every tab with a link straight to the page that fixes it.

optimisation_plan_refused.description:
Smart Home Solutions returned an optimisation plan that this integration will not execute, so no planned device requests are being issued. Measurements are still being uploaded normally.

Reason: {reason}

This usually means the integration needs updating to a build that understands the current plan contract.
